<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Nitiobroges</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Aginnum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the middle Garonne around Agen, whose king Teutomatus fought for Vercingetorix at Gergovia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Nitiobroges lived on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agen">Aginnum</a> (Agen), at the border between the Celtic peoples and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquitani">Aquitani</a>. Caesar notes that their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ollovico">Ollovico</a> had been honoured by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-rome">Roman Senate</a> as a friend.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were ruled by kings in Caesar's day. Their land lay on the river route from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> to the Atlantic, and their coins circulated widely in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ollovico">Ollovico's</a> son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutomatus">Teutomatus</a> joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a> in 52 BCE with cavalry raised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Aquitania</a>; during the attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gergovia">Gergovia</a> he escaped from his tent half-dressed on a wounded horse. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agen">Aginnum</a> became a civitas capital, the origin of Agen.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nitiobroges.jpg" alt="Nitiobroges" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: Feitscherg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Gallia_Tribes_Towns.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aginnum</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ollovico, Teutomatus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=nitiobroges" aria-label="Nitiobroges on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4695 613 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nitiobroges lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5015 869L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5015 869h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5015 869h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Aginnum. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=nitiobroges">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

